WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.865
[MUSIC]

00:00:09.865 --> 00:00:13.780
SPEAKER: Some of the world's greatest
athletes make vast amounts of money.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:19.230
The soccer star Cristiano
Ronaldo makes $80 million a year,

00:00:19.237 --> 00:00:21.683
counting salary and endorsements.

00:00:21.683 --> 00:00:26.169
Basketball great LeBron
James makes $72 million.

00:00:26.169 --> 00:00:30.409
Tiger Woods, the golfer,
earns $61 million in a year.

00:00:30.409 --> 00:00:35.073
And tennis star Roger
Federer makes $56 million.

00:00:35.073 --> 00:00:39.240
Some people argue that rich
people like these sport stars

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.950
should be taxed to help the poor.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:47.830
Others argue that taxation
for redistribution is unjust.

00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:54.612
They say it is admirable for rich people
voluntarily to help people in need

00:00:54.612 --> 00:00:57.949
but wrong for the state
to force them to do so.

00:00:57.949 --> 00:00:59.636
What do you think?

00:00:59.636 --> 00:01:05.322
Is it just or unjust for the state
to tax the rich to help the poor?

00:01:05.322 --> 00:01:09.452
[MUSIC]

